From 58b201afef9389ad501f5c91b7c75902d7a91f41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:10:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/42] network-radio: Radio source on the touchscreen; fix
 network freeze and DMA RAM drain

- Settings drawer: "Radio source" button showing USB / NAS and link state,
  with a panel (NAS address, number keyboard, Use NAS / Use USB / Cancel)
  doing the same as POST /api/relay. Last NAS address kept in NVS.
- wifi.c: the SNTP callback runs on lwIP's tcpip thread, and its QMX time
  push is a CAT write - over the network a socket send that waits on that
  same thread. Every connection froze for good 20-50 s after boot. The time
  work now runs on its own task; radio_relay.c refuses a send from the
  tcpip thread instead of deadlocking.
- New standing patch apply_esp_hosted_sdio_split_psram.ps1: received SDIO
  frames are queued as PSRAM copies; the SDIO mempool never returns memory,
  and frames parked in it drained DMA-capable RAM under the stream.
- mac-capture-serial.sh: note that opening the port restarts the Tab5.
- README and PDF: Radio source control, the fixes, test results, and the
  full power-off cure for a stuck touch controller.

Tested on hardware: NAS -> USB -> NAS from the drawer, QMX+ power cycle at
the NAS (stream resumes), full-rate stream past SNTP with touch working.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
